      {
        "id": 55073,
        "name": "Matchstickman",
        "username": "Matchstickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-13T18:14:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'd go with no, the cards are destroyed because of a trigger on the card, not because of anything La Cappo has done.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>With Fixed Point leaving play I think that is what causes the destruction, not the damage. If it is the damage that causes it then you set a dangerous precedence, Haka would need to track all damage for (currently) indestructible cards reduced to 0HP for Savage Mana, and with the Matriarch/Cohorts &nbsp;around that could be a long time to track a relatively meaningless number.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:29:41.999Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
